## Common Table Expressions (CTEs)

CTEs are temporary named query results created with `WITH`. They help structure complex SQL queries into clear and reusable steps.

### Scenario CTE

Imagine a retail business wants deeper insights from its order data.

The team needs to identify high-value customers, rank orders by revenue, track cumulative sales over time, compare totals within each product group, and find the top-performing order for every product.

These tasks require more than basic filtering and aggregation, so we will use CTEs and window functions to solve them efficiently.

